    "https://www.lr.edu/academics/internships-careers": {
      "title": "Internships & Careers",
      "description": "Internships & Careers | Lenoir-Rhyne University Jump to Header Jump to Main Content Jump to Footer Return to home Open Menu Open Search Search Search Close Search Admission & Aid Click to toggle child links Undergraduate Admission Graduate Admission Seminary Admission Financial Aid & Costs LR Tuition-Free Guarantee College Affordability Paying Your Bill Academics Click to toggle child links Undergraduate Programs Graduate & Doctoral Programs Seminary Programs BEAR Central & Academic Support Research & Scholarship Study Abroad & International Education Internships & Careers Centers & Institutes Registrar Library Student Experience Click to toggle child links Activities & Organizations Athletics Health & Wellness Residence Life Leadership & Service Religious & Spiritual Life Campus Safety Dean of Students Belonging at LR Student Support & Outreach LR Experience Athletics About Click to toggle child links Fast Facts History & Traditions University Leadership Strategic Plan Accreditation Directory Offices & Services Community Partners Resources for Alumni Students Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Apply Visit Request Info Give Close Menu Discover Your Potential Home Page Academics Internships & Careers Internships & Careers Take charge of your potential and your path to career success. When it comes to finding a career that’s right for you, preparation and a strong foundation are key. It's important to take full advantage of all of the resources and opportunities that are available to you in determining your career path. LR faculty and university staff are dedicated to your success. Whether you attend classes in Hickory, Asheville or Columbia or you attend LR online, the same resources and services are available to you through the Career and Professional Development Center. Career & Professional Development Center The Alex Lee Career and Professional Development Center, located in Schaeffer Hall, can help you discover your true personality, explore academic majors and career options, assess your strengths and weaknesses, find internships and part-time work and prepare for life after graduation. The center has partnerships with local companies and organizations to provide opportunities for you to work alongside professionals in the field. As an LR student and graduate, you receive free career counseling for life. So if you are looking for employment, want to update your resume, negotiate a raise or have your eye on a promotion, the center is always available as a resource to prepare you for what is next. View Career & Professional Development Center Internships Education at LR extends beyond the classroom. Through internships, you will connect what you learn in the classroom with real-life applications. You will gain valuable experience while getting an in-depth look at your field of study. Internships Provide Real-World Experience Internships allow you to: Explore career paths and specialties Develop professionalism Understand how workplaces conduct business Learn from seasoned professionals Gain feedback from coworkers and leaders Network with future employers Boost your resume and marketability Internship Opportunities by Major College of Business and Economics Contact the faculty member Accounting, Business, Finance, International Business, Management and Marketing - jamie.conrad@lr.edu College of Education and Human Services Clinical Mental Health Counseling (MA) - astra.czerny@lr.edu (HKY) and patty.hickham@lr.edu (AVL) Elementary Education Coordinator - alyssa.reinhardt@lr.edu Instructional Studies (non-public settings) - hank.weddington@lr.edu Middle Grades Education Coordinator - christopher.gordon@lr.edu School Counseling (MA) - neal.gray@lr.edu Teaching (MAT) - stephanie.woodard@lr.edu College of Fine Arts and Communication Communication Studies - rebecca.alt@lr.edu English - devon.fisher@lr.edu Graphic Design - claire.pope@lr.edu Music - christopher.nigrelli@lr.edu Theatre - lindsay.weitkamp@lr.edu Visual Art - claire.pope@lr.edu College of Health Sciences Community Health (BS) - randall.bergman@lr.edu Dietetic Internship Program - julie.covington@lr.edu Nursing - tabitha.toney@lr.edu Occupational Therapy (MS) - grace.turner@lr.edu Public Health (MPH) - kimberly.price@lr.edu Exercise Science (BS) - ingrid.smith@lr.edu Exercise Science (MS) - amanda.hilton@lr.edu Sports Management - joe.smith@lr.edu College of Humanities and Social Sciences Criminal Justice - robert.stallings@lr.edu Foreign Language - eric.schramm@lr.edu History - paul.custer@lr.edu Political Science, Politics and Law, International Affairs - dustin.berna@lr.edu Psychology - kristen.mayle@lr.edu Religious Studies (for academic credit) - mindy.makant@lr.edu Religious Studies (non-academic credit) - jonathan.schweibert@lr.edu Sociology - katherine.gerlaugh@lr.edu College of Natural Sciences and Mathematics Biochemistry – joshua.ring@lr.edu Biology - scott.schaefer@lr.edu Chemistry - joshua.ring@lr.edu Computer Science - sarah.caudill@lr.edu Engineering Physics - douglas.knight@lr.edu Environmental Science and Policy - john.brzorad@lr.edu Information Technology - sarah.caudill@lr.edu Mathematics - timothy.goldberg@lr.edu Medical Studies - scott.schaefer@lr.edu Natural Sciences - shaun.williams@lr.edu Funding for Internships Lenoir-Rhyne undergraduate students can apply for small grants to help pay for internship-related expenses. You can apply for grants to help cover expenses like temporary housing, commuting costs and work-appropriate clothing. You also can apply for funding to offset lost income while you pursue an unpaid or under-paid internship. As these are intended to be micro-grants, most awards will be in the $100-$750 range. Applications for the 2026-27 academic year are now open. Please submit the form below and note the following: Grants are for currently enrolled undergraduate students only. Applications take 5-10 days for processing. Apply for Internship Funding The Lutheran College Washington Semester provided a real-world work experience for me. It offers the priceless opportunity to work and see D.C. while making important contacts and relationships. Chase Griffin '21, Politics & Law Internships & Careers Career & Professional Development News & Events Mapping a route to entrepreneurship Kevin Miller ’26 turned his love of riding in Western North Carolina into an entrepreneurial venture — with help from LR and a shot at $30,000 in a statewide startup competition. View More Lenoir-Rhyne surpasses $90 million Charge Forward campaign goal ahead of schedule Lenoir-Rhyne University has surpassed the $90 million goal of its Charge Forward comprehensive campaign ahead of schedule, reaching a historic milestone in the largest fundraising campaign in university history. View More View All News September 10 6:30 PM - 8:30 PM / P.E. Monroe Auditorium Visiting Writers Series: Andrew McCarthy October 08 6:30 PM - 7:00 PM / P.E. Monroe Auditorium Visiting Writers Series: Patrick Ryan View All Events Get Info Visit Apply Deposit Return to home Find us on Facebook Subscribe on YouTube Follow us on Instagram 625 7th Ave NE, Hickory, NC 28601 828.328.1741 Directory Virtual Tour, Maps & Directions Events Calendar University News Profile Magazine Work at LR Library Bookstore Copyright Privacy Policy Accessibility Title IX Safety & Emergency Preparedness Consumer Information Coronavirus © 2026 Lenoir-Rhyne University"
