    "https://www.lr.edu/student-experience/dean-of-students": {
      "title": "Dean of Students",
      "description": "Dean of Students | Lenoir-Rhyne University Jump to Header Jump to Main Content Jump to Footer Return to home Open Menu Open Search Search Search Close Search Admission & Aid Click to toggle child links Undergraduate Admission Graduate Admission Seminary Admission Financial Aid & Costs LR Tuition-Free Guarantee College Affordability Paying Your Bill Academics Click to toggle child links Undergraduate Programs Graduate & Doctoral Programs Seminary Programs BEAR Central & Academic Support Research & Scholarship Study Abroad & International Education Internships & Careers Centers & Institutes Registrar Library Student Experience Click to toggle child links Activities & Organizations Athletics Health & Wellness Residence Life Leadership & Service Religious & Spiritual Life Campus Safety Dean of Students Belonging at LR Student Support & Outreach LR Experience Athletics About Click to toggle child links Fast Facts History & Traditions University Leadership Strategic Plan Accreditation Directory Offices & Services Community Partners Resources for Alumni Students Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Apply Visit Request Info Give Close Menu Be engaged & empowered Home Page Student Experience Dean of Students Dean of Students Engaging every student, empowering every journey. The Dean of Students is dedicated to your success—academically, personally and socially. We support your journey at LR through personal connection, student engagement and campus-wide collaboration. Whether through involvement in student life or personalized support, our team is here to help you thrive. If you’d like to connect, reach out anytime at studentlife@lr.edu or visit us on the second floor of the Cromer Center. Follow us on Instagram: @lrustudentlife . Get Involved & Stay Connected At Lenoir-Rhyne, you’re not just earning a degree—you’re building a future through meaningful engagement on campus and beyond. From student organizations and community service to leadership programs and campus events, getting involved helps you develop real-world skills and lifelong friendships. If you are looking to take the next step, we’re here to help you plug in. Visit the links below for more information about student life and opportunities to get involved at LR. Student activities and organizations Leadership and service Religious and spiritual life Residence Life Support When You Need It We know life can bring unexpected challenges. The Dean of Students office offers resources and support when you or your peers are facing difficult situations—whether personal, academic or behavioral. Our goal is to ensure you feel safe, heard and empowered to move forward. Report a Concern We are committed to fostering a respectful and inclusive campus environment. If you witness or experience behavior that is concerning or violates university policies, we encourage you to use one of the confidential reporting tools below. Your voice helps shape a safe and strong LR community. Reporting Resources Student Concern Referral Form Confidential Hazing Report Form Student Conduct Incident Report Form Academic Integrity Violation Student Grievance Report Form Title IX Dean of Students Student Handbook Code of Student Conduct Anti-Hazing Policy & Reporting Student Grievance Policies Missing Student Policy Medical Withdrawal Kate's Cupboard Student Experience Staff Harry Titus Vice President for Student Experience and Dean of Students 625 7th Ave NE, LRU 7484 Hickory, NC 28601 harry.titus@lr.edu 828.328.7246 Staff Page Get Info Visit Apply Deposit Return to home Find us on Facebook Subscribe on YouTube Follow us on Instagram 625 7th Ave NE, Hickory, NC 28601 828.328.1741 Directory Virtual Tour, Maps & Directions Events Calendar University News Profile Magazine Work at LR Library Bookstore Copyright Privacy Policy Accessibility Title IX Safety & Emergency Preparedness Consumer Information Coronavirus © 2026 Lenoir-Rhyne University"
